From 451fd842286179bb19bf3dd1841c5ac6b20787ef Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Niluthon <37350260+Niluthon@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 19 Oct 2026 20:48:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 08/13] B70-0048: fused hot+cold decode MoE op and an FP8 draft
 head

B70_MOE_DECODE_OP=<path to libb70_moe_decode.so> (kernels/b70-moe-decode in the repository; 1 = next to
b70_hotcold.py) runs batches of at most B70_MOE_DECODE_OP_MAX_ROWS (16) tokens through one SYCL op that does the
hot (VRAM) and cold (pinned host, UVA) experts together in three kernels, reading each expert once per layer,
instead of two XpuFusedMoe calls (~56 us fixed cost each before any weight byte). Only for silu without a clamp;
anything else, or a library that does not load, keeps the stock path. Per layer on one B70 (cold share 0.08):
1 row 150 -> 66 us, 4 rows 391 -> 241 us, 8 rows 603 -> 397 us, 16 rows 1030 -> 740 us; rel L2 vs stock ~8e-3.

B70_DRAFT_HEAD_FP8=1: the MTP draft passes use an FP8 (E4M3, per vocab row scale) copy of the lm_head shard via
fp8_gemm_w8a16 (1.08 -> 0.56 ms per pass); the target still verifies with its BF16 head. Built on the first eager
compute_logits call (the memory profile), so KV accounts for it (279,001 -> 271,647 tokens).

Measured on 2x B70, one boot each (op up to 8 rows): 1 stream 61.4 -> 73.1 tok/s (op) -> 76.6 (op + FP8 draft
head), ms/step 45.5 -> 39.3 -> 36.6; code agents at 2 concurrent 90.1 -> 106.5 -> 113.3 tok/s; acceptance unchanged.

Port to 0.32 (from Niluthon/qwen38-flash-tp2@e536e33, Apache-2.0, via our 0.30 carry): conflict in b70_apply_hotcold resolved as: 0.32 sentinel remap of topk_ids, then the fused op or the two stock calls. The op library is the one B70-V32-0054 already loads (same env B70_MOE_DECODE_OP, same b70moe.moe_decode signature; V32-0054 passes the hot weights twice, here the cold arguments are the UVA views). B70_DRAFT_HEAD_FP8 (MTP draft only) finds no BF16 head when B70_HEAD_FP8=1 released it and logs off.
